Patch 49 -- NtCurrentTeb() for the native ARM island must return the GUEST TEB.

On i386, NtCurrentTeb() is `mov fs:0x18` -- Wine's TEB self-pointer, in a segment
Box86 maintains per guest thread. The island compiles the same WineD3D sources
for armhf, where winnt.h's ARM branch reads the coprocessor thread pointer:

    ee1d 2f50   mrc 15, 0, r2, cr13, cr0, {2}
    6a53        ldr r3, [r2, #36]

That is the HOST thread's pointer, which has nothing to do with Wine's TEB.
wined3d_from_cs() identifies the calling thread this way, so every island
function that checks which thread it is on read arbitrary memory.

Measured on the device on 2026-08-15: with the entry marker fixed (patch 48) and
the two window/DC entries dropped, island entry 3, device_invalidate_state,
faulted reading address 0x24 -- the Win32 thread id at TEB+0x24 -- while its
arguments were entirely valid (device=0x02b766d8, state=0x171, read off the
guest stack by the wrapper exactly as intended).

This adds an MGS2_ISLAND_ARM branch that calls mgs2_island_teb(), implemented in
Box86 (src/mgs2_island_natives.c) as the FS base of the current thread's emu
plus 0x18. MGS2_ISLAND_ARM is defined only by
harness/island/full/build_island_objects.sh; the branch is unreachable for the
i386 DLL build, which is not rebuilt.

After this patch the whole binary contains zero `mrc ..., cr13, cr0, {2}`
instructions, and entry 3 runs for a full window without faulting.

diff -ruN old/include/winnt.h new/include/winnt.h
--- old/include/winnt.h	2026-08-15 17:10:22.206704939 +0300
+++ new/include/winnt.h	2026-08-15 17:10:22.179659578 +0300
@@ -2521,12 +2521,28 @@
     return (struct _TEB *)__readgsqword(FIELD_OFFSET(NT_TIB, Self));
 }
 #elif defined(__arm__) && defined(__GNUC__)
+#ifdef MGS2_ISLAND_ARM
+/* Patch 49. The native ARM WineD3D island runs inside Box86, on a host thread,
+ * against a guest process. `mrc p15,0,rX,c13,c0,2` reads the HOST thread
+ * pointer, which has nothing to do with Wine's TEB -- so wined3d_from_cs() and
+ * every other caller that identifies the thread reads arbitrary memory.
+ * Measured: island entry 3 faulted reading TEB+0x24, the Win32 thread id.
+ * Box86 keeps the guest FS base per thread and resolves the TEB from it.
+ * This branch is unreachable for the i386 DLL build, and MGS2_ISLAND_ARM is
+ * defined only by harness/island/full/build_island_objects.sh. */
+struct _TEB * mgs2_island_teb(void);
+static FORCEINLINE struct _TEB * WINAPI NtCurrentTeb(void)
+{
+    return mgs2_island_teb();
+}
+#else
 static FORCEINLINE struct _TEB * WINAPI NtCurrentTeb(void)
 {
     struct _TEB *teb;
     __asm__("mrc p15, 0, %0, c13, c0, 2" : "=r" (teb));
     return teb;
 }
+#endif
 #elif defined(__arm__) && defined(_MSC_VER)
 #pragma intrinsic(_MoveFromCoprocessor)
 static FORCEINLINE struct _TEB * WINAPI NtCurrentTeb(void)
